>> title: Macaroni and Cheese
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: pasta, cheese, baked, southern, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: mac and cheese, macaroni cheese, baked macaroni, macaroni pie, baked mac
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 20 min
>> pairs-with: cheddar-cheese-sauce, collard-greens, fried-chicken, candied-yams

>> step: Bake this rather than stirring a sauce through it: the egg and evaporated milk set to a custard.
Bake this one rather than stirring a sauce through it.

>> step: boil 7 min, drain short of done
Boil @elbow macaroni{1%lb}(450 g) in water with @kosher salt{1%Tbs} for ~boil{7%min}, a minute short of the packet.

>> step: whisk the custard
Whisk @large eggs{3}, @evaporated milk{12%fl oz}(355 mL), @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL), @dry mustard{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @cayenne{1/4%tsp}.

>> step: toss hot with butter and cheese
Toss @&(~2)drained macaroni{} hot with @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g), @sharp cheddar{12%oz}(340 g; coarsely grated).

>> step: pour the custard over
Pour @&(~2)custard{} over @&(~1)dressed macaroni{} in a #9x13-in baking dish{}.

>> step: bake 350°F 45 min
Bake @&(~1)assembled dish{} at 350°F (175°C) under @sharp cheddar{4%oz}(115 g; coarsely grated) for ~bake{45%min}.

Rest it ten minutes before cutting. Straight out of the oven the square will not hold its edge.
